    "summary": "Lively set with strong Good Lovin' and classic China>Rider",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a spirited performance of Hard To Handle, a seamless China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider transition, and two rousing Good Lovin' jams bookended by Turn On Your Lovelight. Jerry’s pedal‑steel cameo during the New Riders set adds a unique touch, while Pigpen’s keyboards shine on Lovelight. Recording quality varies, but the musical highlights make it worth a listen.",
    "review": "On May 3, 1970, the Grateful Dead took over Foss Hill at Wesleyan University for a concert that mixed protest‑era energy with classic Americana. The first set kicked off with a rollicking Hard To Handle before flowing into the beloved China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider pairing, and later erupted into a double Good Lovin' showcase framed by an exuberant Turn On Your Lovelight sandwich around Uncle John's Band. Jerry Garcia slipped in a surprise pedal‑steel line during the New Riders of the Purple Sage segment, and Ron \"Pigpen\" McKernan’s organ work on Lovelight added soulful depth. Although audience recordings are plagued by hiss and occasional buried sections, the performance captures a historic anti‑war vibe and delivers several standout moments that make this show a noteworthy snapshot of early ’70 Dead live energy.",
